    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## Reported security findings\nThese views include **all recommendation and detailed-finding types returned by Azure Resource Graph**, not only recommendations linked to attack paths. There is no fixed list of recommendation IDs or titles, so newer individual vulnerability recommendations are included when published. Healthy, unhealthy, not-applicable, and unknown states remain visible. Connected-cloud records appear when published at the selected subscription scopes.\n\nUse the server-side status selector and search to narrow by assessment state, recommendation, resource ID, vulnerability identifier, or any reported property. **Maximum list rows** defaults to **100**, with options from 25 to 250 and a server-side cap of 250. Compare each list with the server-side totals and narrow the scope or filters when more records match. These lists are bounded views, not a complete paginated export; grid search only filters rows already returned.\n\nLists retain reported severity, first-evaluation timestamps, and a labelled **512-character remediation preview** with a truncation flag, but do not bulk-load raw context objects. **Select a row** to load complete remediation and context below, including the entire properties object as JSON rather than a fixed selection of fields. This avoids returning large raw payloads for hundreds of records at once. Use selected-context exports when full remediation or raw context is required. **No findings does not prove that a capability is enabled, supported, scanned, or healthy.**\n\nSettings cannot reliably identify which extension produced a finding, so these views do not guess feature ownership from titles. API endpoint sensitive-information details, Cloud Security Explorer graph insights, and some serverless vulnerability experiences are available only in the product portals, not universally through Resource Graph. Use [API security findings](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/enable-api-security-posture), [serverless protection](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/serverless-protection), and [serverless container posture](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/posture-for-serverless-containers) for those investigations. Context data can be sensitive; review access and content before exporting."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "tab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "findings"
      },
      "name": "all_findings_guidance"
    },
    {
      "type": 9,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "id": "2118368a-f05e-4d21-9672-0fc0a1cefa9f",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "FindingStatus",
            "label": "Assessment status (server-side)",
            "type": 2,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": "All",
            "jsonData": "[{\"value\":\"All\",\"label\":\"All states\"},{\"value\":\"Unhealthy\",\"label\":\"Unhealthy\"},{\"value\":\"Healthy\",\"label\":\"Healthy\"},{\"value\":\"NotApplicable\",\"label\":\"Not applicable\"},{\"value\":\"Other\",\"label\":\"Other or unknown state\"}]"
          },
          {
            "id": "09bff57e-4e7e-4863-9bc5-27714d67a9dc",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "FindingSearch",
            "label": "Findings search (server-side)",
            "type": 1,
            "isRequired": false,
            "value": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "a40ac234-c797-490f-9f31-05b5ed131d85",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "FindingLimit",
            "label": "Maximum list rows",
            "type": 2,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": "100",
            "jsonData": "[{\"value\":\"25\",\"label\":\"25\"},{\"value\":\"50\",\"label\":\"50\"},{\"value\":\"100\",\"label\":\"100\"},{\"value\":\"250\",\"label\":\"250\"}]"
          }
        ],
        "style": "above",
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources"
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "tab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "findings"
      },
      "name": "findings_search"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "title": "Server-side finding totals for this scope and search",
        "query": "securityresources\n| where type in~ (\"microsoft.security/assessments\", \"microsoft.security/assessments/subassessments\")\n| where \"{FindingStatus:escape}\" == \"All\" or tostring(properties.status.code) =~ \"{FindingStatus:escape}\"\n    or (\"{FindingStatus:escape}\" == \"Other\" and tostring(properties.status.code) !in~ (\"Unhealthy\", \"Healthy\", \"NotApplicable\"))\n| where isempty(\"{FindingSearch:escape}\") or id contains \"{FindingSearch:escape}\" or tostring(properties) contains \"{FindingSearch:escape}\"\n| extend FindingType = iff(type =~ \"microsoft.security/assessments\", \"Recommendations\", \"Detailed findings\")\n| summarize Total = count(), Unhealthy = countif(properties.status.code =~ \"Unhealthy\"),\n    Healthy = countif(properties.status.code =~ \"Healthy\"), NotApplicable = countif(properties.status.code =~ \"NotApplicable\"),\n    OtherOrUnknown = countif(tostring(properties.status.code) !in~ (\"Unhealthy\", \"Healthy\", \"NotApplicable\")) by FindingType\n| extend DisplayLimit = min_of(250, toint(\"{FindingLimit:escape}\"))\n| extend Notice = iff(Total > DisplayLimit, \"More records match than the list limit. Narrow subscriptions, status, or search; selected-record details load separately.\", \"Compare these totals with displayed rows. No data does not prove coverage.\")\n| order by FindingType asc",
        "size": 1,
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{subscriptions}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table",
        "noDataMessage": "No assessment records matched this scope and search. Check access, data availability, and the search; this is not evidence of healthy coverage.",
        "gridSettings": {
          "filter": true,
          "rowLimit": 1000,
          "formatters": [],
          "labelSettings": [
            {
              "columnId": "FindingType",
              "label": "Record type"
            },
            {
              "columnId": "Total",
              "label": "Total matching records"
            },
            {
              "columnId": "Unhealthy",
              "label": "Unhealthy"
            },
            {
              "columnId": "Healthy",
              "label": "Healthy"
            },
            {
              "columnId": "NotApplicable",
              "label": "Not applicable"
            },
            {
              "columnId": "OtherOrUnknown",
              "label": "Other or unknown state"
            },
            {
              "columnId": "DisplayLimit",
              "label": "List row limit"
            },
            {
              "columnId": "Notice",
              "label": "Completeness guidance"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "tab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "findings"
      },
      "name": "findings_counts",
      "styleSettings": {
        "showBorder": true
      }
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "title": "Reported recommendations - select a row for full context",
        "query": "securityresources\n| where type =~ \"microsoft.security/assessments\"\n| where \"{FindingStatus:escape}\" == \"All\" or tostring(properties.status.code) =~ \"{FindingStatus:escape}\"\n    or (\"{FindingStatus:escape}\" == \"Other\" and tostring(properties.status.code) !in~ (\"Unhealthy\", \"Healthy\", \"NotApplicable\"))\n| where isempty(\"{FindingSearch:escape}\") or id contains \"{FindingSearch:escape}\" or tostring(properties) contains \"{FindingSearch:escape}\"\n| extend Recommendation = coalesce(tostring(properties.displayName), tostring(properties.metadata.displayName), \"Not reported\"), Status = coalesce(tostring(properties.status.code), \"Not reported\"),\n    Severity = coalesce(tostring(properties.metadata.severity), tostring(properties.additionalData.Severity), tostring(properties.additionalData.severity), \"Not reported\"), RiskLevel = coalesce(tostring(properties.risk.level), \"Not reported\")\n| extend statusOrder = case(Status =~ \"Unhealthy\", 0, Status =~ \"Healthy\", 2, Status =~ \"NotApplicable\", 3, 1), riskOrder = case(RiskLevel =~ \"Critical\", 0, RiskLevel =~ \"High\", 1, RiskLevel =~ \"Medium\", 2, RiskLevel =~ \"Low\", 3, 4), severityOrder = case(Severity =~ \"Critical\", 0, Severity =~ \"High\", 1, Severity =~ \"Medium\", 2, Severity =~ \"Low\", 3, 4)\n| order by statusOrder asc, riskOrder asc, severityOrder asc, Recommendation asc, id asc\n| take toint(\"{FindingLimit:escape}\")\n| take 250\n| extend fullRemediation = coalesce(tostring(properties.metadata.remediationDescription), tostring(properties.additionalData.RemediationDescription), tostring(properties.additionalData.remediationDescription), \"Not reported\")\n| project subscriptionId, Recommendation, Status, Severity, RiskLevel, Source = coalesce(tostring(properties.resourceDetails.Source), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.source), \"Not reported\"),\n    ResourceId = coalesce(tostring(properties.resourceDetails.Id), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.id), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.NativeResourceId), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.AwsResourceId), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.GcpResourceId)), Remediation = substring(fullRemediation, 0, 512), RemediationTruncated = strlen(fullRemediation) > 512,\n    FirstEvaluated = todatetime(properties.status.firstEvaluationDate),\n    RecommendationId = name, AssessmentId = id, PortalLink = tostring(properties.links.azurePortal)",
        "size": 1,
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{subscriptions}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table",
